    {
      "start": 120.76800000000368,
      "end": 239.9280000000073
    },
    {
      "start": 239.9280000000073,
      "end": 378.0480000000116
    },
    {
      "start": 378.0480000000116,
      "end": 509.9520000000157
    },
    {
      "start": 509.9520000000157,
      "end": 641.6640000000198
    },
    {
      "start": 641.6640000000198,
      "end": 786.4800000000243
    }
  ],
  "cues": [
    {
      "start": 0,
      "end": 1.7400000095367432,
      "text": "Hey, welcome back.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 2.299999952316284,
      "end": 4.840000152587891,
      "text": "You already know how to describe motion along a straight line.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 5.699999809265137,
      "end": 9.5,
      "text": "Today we let motion turn corners, change observers, and leave the ground.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 10.15999984741211,
      "end": 14.020000457763672,
      "text": "Our tools are still position, velocity, acceleration, and time.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 14.699999809265137,
      "end": 16.3799991607666,
      "text": "We just need to keep direction in the picture.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 17.15999984741211,
      "end": 19.979999542236328,
      "text": "Choose east as positive x and north as positive y.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 20.579999923706055,
      "end": 25.059999465942383,
      "text": "A velocity with components three meters per second east and four north has",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 25.059999465942383,
      "end": 26.84000015258789,
      "text": "speed five, not seven.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 26.84000015258789,
      "end": 30.34000015258789,
      "text": "The components are perpendicular, so their squared values add.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 31.1200008392334,
      "end": 33.41999816894531,
      "text": "The direction is about fifty three degrees north of east.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 34.65999984741211,
      "end": 37.7400016784668,
      "text": "Components carry signs; the speed is the nonnegative magnitude.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 38.58000183105469,
      "end": 40.97999954223633,
      "text": "Now imagine watching a faster bus from a slower bus.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 41.70000076293945,
      "end": 45.060001373291016,
      "text": "The ground measures their velocities as eighteen and twelve meters per second",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 45.060001373291016,
      "end": 45.400001525878906,
      "text": "east.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 46.52000045776367,
      "end": 48.02000045776367,
      "text": "What speed does the slower bus see?",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 48.70000076293945,
      "end": 49.31999969482422,
      "text": "Take a moment.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 50.02000045776367,
      "end": 51.380001068115234,
      "text": "Six meters per second east.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 52.619998931884766,
      "end": 56.099998474121094,
      "text": "Relative position means the position of A minus the position of B.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 56.97999954223633,
      "end": 61.5,
      "text": "Differentiating that difference gives relative velocity: velocity of A minus",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 61.5,
      "end": 62.2599983215332,
      "text": "velocity of B.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 62.880001068115234,
      "end": 66.18000030517578,
      "text": "This subtraction works component by component, not just along a road.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 66.87999725341797,
      "end": 70.13999938964844,
      "text": "If the faster vehicle starts one hundred twenty meters behind the slower one",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 70.5199966430664,
      "end": 74.69999694824219,
      "text": "and both velocities stay constant, that gap closes at six meters per second.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 75.45999908447266,
      "end": 78.91999816894531,
      "text": "Catch up time is one hundred twenty divided by six, or twenty seconds.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 79.5,
      "end": 83.91999816894531,
      "text": "If B instead moves west at twelve, its signed velocity is negative twelve.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 83.91999816894531,
      "end": 86.69999694824219,
      "text": "Subtracting it gives thirty meters per second east.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 87.41999816894531,
      "end": 90.9000015258789,
      "text": "The familiar add the speeds shortcut is really signed vector subtraction.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 91.9800033569336,
      "end": 95.54820681840945,
      "text": "For two trains travelling east at eighteen and twelve, with lengths one",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 95.54820681840945,
      "end": 95.9000015258789,
      "text": "hundred",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 95.9000015258789,
      "end": 100.16000366210938,
      "text": "and one hundred forty meters, complete overtaking from first overlap to last",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 100.16000366210938,
      "end": 103.12000274658203,
      "text": "overlap requires two hundred forty meters of relative travel.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 103.87999725341797,
      "end": 108.08000183105469,
      "text": "That takes forty seconds, assuming parallel tracks and constant velocities.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 108.95999908447266,
      "end": 112.81999969482422,
      "text": "A point catching a point and a whole train passing another train are different",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 112.81999969482422,
      "end": 113.73999786376953,
      "text": "geometry questions.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 114.58000183105469,
      "end": 118.80000305175781,
      "text": "In a JEE style problem, draw the initial separation before choosing what",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 118.80000305175781,
      "end": 120.4800033569336,
      "text": "distance to divide by relative speed.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 120.76800000000368,
      "end": 123.82799994278322,
      "text": "Let's take the same observer idea to a river.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 124.6279998950995,
      "end": 125.72800003815065,
      "text": "Here is our original example.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 126.48799979019533,
      "end": 129.90800034332642,
      "text": "The banks are one hundred twenty meters apart, measured northward.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 130.98800026703248,
      "end": 132.98800026703248,
      "text": "Water flows east at three meters per second.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 133.74799954224,
      "end": 136.70799958038697,
      "text": "A boat can maintain five meters per second relative to the water.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 137.82799946594605,
      "end": 139.96800076294312,
      "text": "Ignore changes in current and the time taken to turn.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 140.72799908447632,
      "end": 145.14799916077027,
      "text": "The boat's ground velocity is its velocity relative to water plus the water's",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 145.14799916077027,
      "end": 146.42799984741578,
      "text": "velocity relative to ground.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 147.28800045776734,
      "end": 151.5679992370642,
      "text": "Picture walking across a moving walkway: your own motion and the walkway's",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 151.5679992370642,
      "end": 152.84800183105835,
      "text": "motion both contribute.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 154.16800152588257,
      "end": 155.22799908447632,
      "text": "First, aim the boat due north.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 156.00800167847046,
      "end": 160.15876927381052,
      "text": "The ground velocity then has a north component of five and an east component",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 160.15876927381052,
      "end": 160.26800000000367,
      "text": "of",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 160.26800000000367,
      "end": 160.5679992370642,
      "text": "three.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 161.808000915531,
      "end": 165.04799877930054,
      "text": "Crossing time depends on the north component because that is the direction of",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 165.04799877930054,
      "end": 165.72799908447632,
      "text": "the river's width.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 165.72799908447632,
      "end": 169.94800030517945,
      "text": "One hundred twenty divided by five gives twenty four seconds.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 170.72799908447632,
      "end": 174.1480010681189,
      "text": "During that time, the current carries the boat seventy two meters east.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 175.20799862671265,
      "end": 178.62800061035523,
      "text": "This is the minimum crossing time for the given boat speed and a current",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 178.62800061035523,
      "end": 179.60800015259156,
      "text": "parallel to the banks.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 180.60800015259156,
      "end": 180.88799893188843,
      "text": "Why?",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 181.0679992370642,
      "end": 185.0079978637732,
      "text": "The largest possible north component of a five meter per second velocity is",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 185.0079978637732,
      "end": 185.3880027465857,
      "text": "five.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 185.9079993896521,
      "end": 188.6079963378943,
      "text": "Any upstream tilt makes that component smaller.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 189.76800000000367,
      "end": 190.5879996948279,
      "text": "Now change the goal.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 191.14799725342164,
      "end": 193.86799847412476,
      "text": "We want to reach the point directly opposite our starting point.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 193.86799847412476,
      "end": 195.64799725342164,
      "text": "Should we still aim north?",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 196.34800183105835,
      "end": 197.66800152588257,
      "text": "Think about the current for a moment.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 198.70800244140992,
      "end": 198.82799755859742,
      "text": "No.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 199.32799755859742,
      "end": 202.55876678936664,
      "text": "Aim upstream so the boat's westward component relative to water is three",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 202.55876678936664,
      "end": 202.82799755859742,
      "text": "meters",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 202.82799755859742,
      "end": 203.34800183105835,
      "text": "per second.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 204.1079963378943,
      "end": 205.9079993896521,
      "text": "It cancels the current's eastward three.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 206.32799755859742,
      "end": 211.0079978637732,
      "text": "The boat's own speed is still five, so its north component is the square root",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 211.0079978637732,
      "end": 214.02800213623414,
      "text": "of twenty five minus nine: four meters per second.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 214.82799755859742,
      "end": 216.54799877930054,
      "text": "The crossing now takes thirty seconds.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 217.308000915531,
      "end": 220.87415089612497,
      "text": "The upstream heading makes about thirty seven degrees with north, since sine",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 220.87415089612497,
      "end": 220.96799694824585,
      "text": "of",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 220.96799694824585,
      "end": 222.76800000000367,
      "text": "that angle is three divided by five.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 223.6079963378943,
      "end": 227.06800305176148,
      "text": "Minimum time and zero drift are different instructions, not competing answers",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 227.06800305176148,
      "end": 227.94800030517945,
      "text": "to the same question.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 228.6079963378943,
      "end": 232.3838969585749,
      "text": "In this ideal model, directly opposite landing requires boat speed greater",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 232.3838969585749,
      "end": 232.5879996948279,
      "text": "than",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 232.5879996948279,
      "end": 233.0879996948279,
      "text": "current speed.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 233.8880027465857,
      "end": 237.76800000000367,
      "text": "Equal speeds leave no north component when the current is canceled.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 237.76800000000367,
      "end": 239.8155002288878,
      "text": "Read the requested destination before calculating, and always label the frame",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 239.8155002288878,
      "end": 239.9280000000073,
      "text": "of each velocity.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 239.9280000000073,
      "end": 244.04799988556638,
      "text": "A ball follows a curved path, but our equations do not have to become",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 244.04799988556638,
      "end": 244.62799980927244,
      "text": "mysterious.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 245.66799977112547,
      "end": 248.2079997329785,
      "text": "Split its motion into horizontal and vertical components.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 249.28799965668455,
      "end": 253.88800003815427,
      "text": "We assume a uniform downward gravitational field and neglect air resistance.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 255.22800019074216,
      "end": 257.88799908447993,
      "text": "After launch, gravity is the only acceleration.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 258.88799908447993,
      "end": 263.3480000763012,
      "text": "Choose the launch point as origin, positive x horizontally, and positive y",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 263.3480000763012,
      "end": 263.6880002288891,
      "text": "upward.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 264.4079995422436,
      "end": 268.78800061035884,
      "text": "For speed u at angle theta above the horizontal, the initial horizontal",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 268.78800061035884,
      "end": 271.14799931336177,
      "text": "component is u times cosine theta.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 272.2479996948315,
      "end": 274.6280007629467,
      "text": "The vertical component is u times sine theta.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 275.6480012207104,
      "end": 279.16800167847407,
      "text": "Horizontal acceleration is zero, so horizontal velocity stays constant.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 280.44800045777095,
      "end": 283.86799862671626,
      "text": "Vertical acceleration is negative g, so vertical velocity changes.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 284.8080010681225,
      "end": 286.6879983215405,
      "text": "Both directions share the same elapsed time.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 286.7479996948315,
      "end": 288.0679993896557,
      "text": "That is what connects them.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 288.9280000000073,
      "end": 292.5031279195222,
      "text": "Horizontal displacement is the initial horizontal component multiplied by",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 292.5031279195222,
      "end": 292.7479996948315,
      "text": "time.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 293.3479981689526,
      "end": 297.2479996948315,
      "text": "Vertical displacement is the initial vertical component multiplied by time,",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 297.70799877930415,
      "end": 299.60800030518305,
      "text": "minus one half g times time squared.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 300.52799847412837,
      "end": 304.3280015258862,
      "text": "Let's launch an ideal ball at twenty meters per second, thirty degrees above",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 304.3280015258862,
      "end": 304.7479996948315,
      "text": "horizontal.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 305.6480012207104,
      "end": 308.68800213623774,
      "text": "Use g equal to ten meters per second squared for this example.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 309.487997558601,
      "end": 313.28800061035884,
      "text": "Its horizontal component is ten square root of three, and its vertical",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 313.28800061035884,
      "end": 314.3479981689526,
      "text": "component is ten.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 315.12799694824946,
      "end": 317.6480012207104,
      "text": "At the top, vertical velocity becomes zero.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 318.4680009155346,
      "end": 322.28800061035884,
      "text": "Ten minus ten times t equals zero, giving one second to reach the top.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 322.9280000000073,
      "end": 323.6480012207104,
      "text": "Has the ball stopped?",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 324.12799694824946,
      "end": 324.6679978637768,
      "text": "Take a moment.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 325.40800335694087,
      "end": 326.9479966430737,
      "text": "Only its vertical component has stopped.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 327.52799847412837,
      "end": 330.70799877930415,
      "text": "Its horizontal velocity is still ten square root of three.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 331.4280000000073,
      "end": 332.90800335694087,
      "text": "Acceleration is still ten downward.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 333.60800030518305,
      "end": 338.20799877930415,
      "text": "The maximum height above launch is ten squared divided by twice ten, or five",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 338.20799877930415,
      "end": 338.4680009155346,
      "text": "meters.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 339.0679993896557,
      "end": 343.3680024414135,
      "text": "If the ball lands at its launch height, the nonzero root of zero equals ten t",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 343.3680024414135,
      "end": 345.60800030518305,
      "text": "minus five t squared is two seconds.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 346.5679993896557,
      "end": 350.30799725342524,
      "text": "Multiply that time by the horizontal component to get a range of twenty square",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 350.30799725342524,
      "end": 352.7679963378979,
      "text": "root of three meters, about thirty four point six.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 353.6679978637768,
      "end": 356.3280015258862,
      "text": "Eliminating time gives a downward opening parabolic trajectory.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 357.1480012207104,
      "end": 360.7110787071888,
      "text": "The curve comes from horizontal motion proportional to time and vertical",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 360.7110787071888,
      "end": 361.00800183106196,
      "text": "motion",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 361.00800183106196,
      "end": 362.0679993896557,
      "text": "containing time squared.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 362.7280030517651,
      "end": 367.65107527982997,
      "text": "For same height landing, time of flight is twice u sine theta divided by g,",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 367.65107527982997,
      "end": 367.8479981689526,
      "text": "and",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 367.8479981689526,
      "end": 370.7280030517651,
      "text": "range is u squared sine twice theta divided by g.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 371.4679932861401,
      "end": 375.0280061035229,
      "text": "Those shortcuts require the stated ideal model and equal launch and landing",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 375.0280061035229,
      "end": 375.2679963378979,
      "text": "heights.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 375.8479981689526,
      "end": 377.6879945068432,
      "text": "They are not universal projectile formulas.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 378.0480000000116,
      "end": 380.5679999809381,
      "text": "Now the landing point is below the launch point.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 381.32799997140137,
      "end": 384.9144100628749,
      "text": "This is where memorized same height formulas can quietly give the wrong",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 384.9144100628749,
      "end": 385.26799979020325,
      "text": "answer.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 386.50800003815857,
      "end": 390.61825637994605,
      "text": "Imagine an ideal horizontal launch at fifteen meters per second from a",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 390.61825637994605,
      "end": 391.0879999618646,
      "text": "platform",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 391.0879999618646,
      "end": 393.2280003051874,
      "text": "twenty meters above the landing surface.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 394.28799977112976,
      "end": 396.7679993133661,
      "text": "Use g equal to ten and ignore air resistance.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 397.84799923707214,
      "end": 400.34799923707214,
      "text": "Put the origin at launch and keep upward positive.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 401.168000839245,
      "end": 402.7679993133661,
      "text": "Initial vertical velocity is zero.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 403.5279995422479,
      "end": 407.96800007630554,
      "text": "At landing, y is negative twenty, not positive twenty.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 407.96800007630554,
      "end": 412.16799893189636,
      "text": "Our vertical equation becomes negative twenty equals negative five t squared.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 413.08800091553894,
      "end": 417.68799938966004,
      "text": "Time is two seconds; discard the negative root because we are asking about the",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 417.68799938966004,
      "end": 418.42800106812683,
      "text": "event after launch.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 419.68799938966004,
      "end": 422.7680012207147,
      "text": "Horizontal displacement is fifteen times two, or thirty meters.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 423.7880016784784,
      "end": 427.7680012207147,
      "text": "Notice why increasing horizontal launch speed would increase range without",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 427.7680012207147,
      "end": 429.6479984741327,
      "text": "changing falling time in this ideal model.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 430.4879986267206,
      "end": 434.08800091553894,
      "text": "The vertical drop and vertical initial velocity have not changed.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 435.00799908448425,
      "end": 439.2079998474237,
      "text": "At impact, horizontal velocity is still positive fifteen.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 439.2079998474237,
      "end": 441.7280003051874,
      "text": "Vertical velocity is negative twenty.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 441.7280003051874,
      "end": 445.8480030517694,
      "text": "The speed is the square root of fifteen squared plus twenty squared, giving",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 445.8480030517694,
      "end": 447.3679996948358,
      "text": "twenty five meters per second.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 448.2479969482538,
      "end": 451.18799938966004,
      "text": "The direction is about fifty three degrees below horizontal.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 451.6479984741327,
      "end": 454.8279987793085,
      "text": "We do not add fifteen and twenty as scalar speeds.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 455.5280033569452,
      "end": 456.90800061036316,
      "text": "Those components are perpendicular.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 457.78799786378113,
      "end": 461.90800061036316,
      "text": "For an angled launch from a height, use y equals initial vertical velocity",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 461.90800061036316,
      "end": 466.92799725342957,
      "text": "times t minus one half g t squared, and set y to the actual signed landing",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 466.92799725342957,
      "end": 467.2280003051874,
      "text": "height.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 468.0280033569452,
      "end": 471.73415634625934,
      "text": "A quadratic can have two positive roots if the projectile passes a raised",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 471.73415634625934,
      "end": 471.98800244141785,
      "text": "level",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 471.98800244141785,
      "end": 473.80800213624207,
      "text": "once upward and again downward.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 474.60799755860535,
      "end": 476.9480015258905,
      "text": "The situation tells you which event is requested.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 477.8279987793085,
      "end": 481.8480030517694,
      "text": "There is one useful range result worth understanding: at fixed launch speed,",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 482.16800274659363,
      "end": 486.208003662121,
      "text": "with the same launch and landing height, range depends on sine of twice the",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 486.208003662121,
      "end": 486.6479984741327,
      "text": "launch angle.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 487.5280033569452,
      "end": 489.48800244141785,
      "text": "It is largest at forty five degrees.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 490.30800213624207,
      "end": 493.67007241717215,
      "text": "Complementary angles have equal ranges but generally different flight times",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 493.67007241717215,
      "end": 494.208003662121,
      "text": "and heights.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 495.00799908448425,
      "end": 499.00799908448425,
      "text": "For different height landing, neither that equal range symmetry nor forty five",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 499.00799908448425,
      "end": 501.2479969482538,
      "text": "degrees as the optimum is generally valid.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 502.0280033569452,
      "end": 505.1479984741327,
      "text": "In JEE practice, first write the physical landing condition.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 505.8279987793085,
      "end": 509.22799267579285,
      "text": "Let the equation choose the time instead of making the scene fit a remembered",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 509.22799267579285,
      "end": 509.6480061035272,
      "text": "shortcut.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 509.9520000000157,
      "end": 513.3320001144566,
      "text": "Constant speed does not always mean zero acceleration.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 514.0919998665013,
      "end": 515.6719997902073,
      "text": "Watch a point moving around a circle.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 516.0319999237217,
      "end": 520.0920003433384,
      "text": "At the rightmost point, an anticlockwise moving point has upward velocity.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 520.8720000763096,
      "end": 522.9919999618687,
      "text": "A little later, its velocity tilts left.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 523.5920003433384,
      "end": 527.0319999237217,
      "text": "The speed can stay the same while the velocity vector changes direction.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 527.7120002288975,
      "end": 529.5919993896641,
      "text": "That change requires acceleration.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 530.4520000000157,
      "end": 534.5919993896641,
      "text": "For uniform circular motion, acceleration points toward the center, while",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 534.5919993896641,
      "end": 536.2719996948399,
      "text": "velocity is tangent to the path.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 536.8720000763096,
      "end": 540.8120006103672,
      "text": "Over a very short interval, the little triangle formed by the velocity change",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 540.8120006103672,
      "end": 544.2519992370762,
      "text": "is similar to the triangle formed by two nearby radius vectors.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 545.0919993896641,
      "end": 549.2319987793126,
      "text": "The magnitude of the velocity change divided by speed is approximately the",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 549.2319987793126,
      "end": 551.2319987793126,
      "text": "traveled arc length divided by radius.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 552.0120013733067,
      "end": 554.2719996948399,
      "text": "Divide by the short time interval and take its limit.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 554.8919986267247,
      "end": 558.3520015258946,
      "text": "The inward acceleration becomes speed squared divided by radius.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 558.9119990844883,
      "end": 563.2135374051765,
      "text": "This is a kinematic result; a later force analysis identifies which real",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 563.2135374051765,
      "end": 563.5719989319005,
      "text": "forces",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 563.5719989319005,
      "end": 564.1520007629551,
      "text": "supply it.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 564.7119983215489,
      "end": 568.1720012207188,
      "text": "Angular speed omega means angle turned per second in radians.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 569.0919993896641,
      "end": 573.1320003051915,
      "text": "Arc length equals radius times angle, so speed equals omega times radius.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 573.8919986267247,
      "end": 578.2319987793126,
      "text": "One revolution covers two pi radians and takes a period of two pi divided by",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 578.2319987793126,
      "end": 578.4119990844883,
      "text": "omega.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 579.2319987793126,
      "end": 582.3920024414219,
      "text": "Suppose radius is two meters and speed is four meters per second.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 583.0919993896641,
      "end": 587.5720027465977,
      "text": "Omega is two radians per second, period is pi seconds, and inward acceleration",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 587.5720027465977,
      "end": 589.2120021362462,
      "text": "is eight meters per second squared.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 589.992000915543,
      "end": 594.2719996948399,
      "text": "After half a revolution, distance traveled is two pi meters, but displacement",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 594.2719996948399,
      "end": 596.371998168961,
      "text": "magnitude is the diameter, four meters.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 597.2520030517735,
      "end": 598.4719966430821,
      "text": "Average speed remains four.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 599.0320018310704,
      "end": 602.8319972534337,
      "text": "Average velocity magnitude is displacement divided by half period: eight",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 602.8319972534337,
      "end": 604.5720027465977,
      "text": "divided by pi meters per second.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 605.2919963379063,
      "end": 606.5119975586094,
      "text": "Now let the point speed up.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 606.9719966430821,
      "end": 610.5720027465977,
      "text": "It still needs radial acceleration to turn, and it also has tangential",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 610.5720027465977,
      "end": 612.0119975586094,
      "text": "acceleration to change speed.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 612.8319972534337,
      "end": 617.3120006103672,
      "text": "At the instant when speed is four and radius is two, radial acceleration is",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 617.3120006103672,
      "end": 617.6120036621251,
      "text": "eight.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 618.1919978637852,
      "end": 622.8120006103672,
      "text": "If tangential acceleration is six, total acceleration magnitude is ten, from",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 622.8120006103672,
      "end": 625.8319972534337,
      "text": "the square root of sixty four plus thirty six.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 625.8319972534337,
      "end": 629.8120006103672,
      "text": "The two components are perpendicular; their scalar magnitudes must not simply",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 629.8120006103672,
      "end": 630.4320033569493,
      "text": "be added.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 631.0720027465977,
      "end": 633.5919993896641,
      "text": "Always use instantaneous speed in the radial formula.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 634.5720027465977,
      "end": 638.5520061035313,
      "text": "Uniform circular motion has constant angular speed, not constant velocity.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 638.9520000000157,
      "end": 641.4720042724766,
      "text": "That distinction is a common conceptual test.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 641.6640000000198,
      "end": 646.3239998474319,
      "text": "Let's finish with a problem that refuses to use constant acceleration.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 647.1040000572402,
      "end": 652.4640001907546,
      "text": "A particle's position in meters is t cubed minus six t squared plus nine t,",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 652.4640001907546,
      "end": 653.56399961855,
      "text": "with time in seconds.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 654.5040001526077,
      "end": 657.4640001907546,
      "text": "The numerical coefficients carry the corresponding SI units.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 658.3640007629592,
      "end": 660.2640003814895,
      "text": "We study time from zero to three seconds.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 661.06399961855,
      "end": 664.8239998474319,
      "text": "Instantaneous velocity is the slope of the position time graph, so",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 664.8239998474319,
      "end": 665.8239998474319,
      "text": "differentiate position.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 667.0240006103713,
      "end": 670.06399961855,
      "text": "Velocity is three t squared minus twelve t plus nine.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 670.6439995422561,
      "end": 675.2040009155471,
      "text": "Differentiate again: acceleration is six t minus twelve.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 675.2040009155471,
      "end": 678.6039986267288,
      "text": "Because acceleration changes with time, do not use the constant acceleration",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 678.6039986267288,
      "end": 679.983999694844,
      "text": "equations over the whole journey.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 680.8440003051956,
      "end": 684.4639992370803,
      "text": "Factor the velocity as three times t minus one times t minus three.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 685.423998321553,
      "end": 688.983999694844,
      "text": "It is positive from zero to one second and negative from one to three.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 690.0040001526077,
      "end": 691.8239998474319,
      "text": "The particle turns around at one second.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 692.3440003051956,
      "end": 695.9439987793166,
      "text": "At three seconds it reaches zero velocity again, at our interval's endpoint.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 696.7440018310745,
      "end": 700.3239998474319,
      "text": "Now calculate position at the boundaries and at the interior turning point.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 701.5040001526077,
      "end": 702.6039986267288,
      "text": "Position at zero is zero.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 703.6439995422561,
      "end": 704.8440003051956,
      "text": "Position at one is four meters.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 705.9439987793166,
      "end": 707.3240036621291,
      "text": "Position at three is zero again.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 708.2639984741409,
      "end": 709.3039993896682,
      "text": "What is the total distance?",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 709.9439987793166,
      "end": 711.6640000000198,
      "text": "Take a moment to separate it from displacement.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 712.6440033569534,
      "end": 717.3039993896682,
      "text": "The particle goes from zero to four, then from four back to zero: eight meters",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 717.3039993896682,
      "end": 717.7239975586135,
      "text": "traveled.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 718.7840027466018,
      "end": 719.483999694844,
      "text": "Displacement is zero.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 720.104002441426,
      "end": 724.1440033569534,
      "text": "Its average velocity over three seconds is zero, but average speed is eight",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 724.1440033569534,
      "end": 725.7239975586135,
      "text": "divided by three meters per second.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 727.0640015258987,
      "end": 731.140922548754,
      "text": "The positive and negative areas under the velocity time curve are plus four",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 731.140922548754,
      "end": 731.3039993896682,
      "text": "and",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 731.3039993896682,
      "end": 732.0640015258987,
      "text": "minus four meters.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 732.9640030517776,
      "end": 735.2040009155471,
      "text": "That signed area check agrees with the positions.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 736.0640015258987,
      "end": 740.1793849675303,
      "text": "At two seconds, acceleration is zero, but velocity is negative three meters",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 740.1793849675303,
      "end": 740.3440003051956,
      "text": "per",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 740.3440003051956,
      "end": 740.5839981689651,
      "text": "second.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 741.483999694844,
      "end": 743.8840012207229,
      "text": "Zero acceleration at an instant does not mean rest.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 744.6440033569534,
      "end": 748.6440033569534,
      "text": "Before that instant, velocity and acceleration are both negative, so speed",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 748.6440033569534,
      "end": 749.104002441426,
      "text": "increases.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 749.104002441426,
      "end": 754.0240006103713,
      "text": "After it, velocity is negative while acceleration is positive, so speed",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 754.0240006103713,
      "end": 754.5640015258987,
      "text": "decreases.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 755.5240006103713,
      "end": 759.6839966430862,
      "text": "For a position graph, slope gives velocity; for a velocity graph, slope gives",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 759.6839966430862,
      "end": 762.0839981689651,
      "text": "acceleration and signed area gives displacement.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 763.0439972534377,
      "end": 766.5640015258987,
      "text": "For an acceleration graph, signed area gives change in velocity, not",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 766.5640015258987,
      "end": 767.0240006103713,
      "text": "displacement.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 767.9439987793166,
      "end": 770.6927141066528,
      "text": "This class adds the main missing motion models to our straight line",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 770.6927141066528,
      "end": 771.1439957275588,
      "text": "foundation.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 771.9439987793166,
      "end": 775.9040054931838,
      "text": "More multi stage projectile, relative motion and calculus practice still",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 775.9040054931838,
      "end": 776.6840042724807,
      "text": "belongs in revision.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 777.2839951172073,
      "end": 781.2839951172073,
      "text": "Choose the frame, identify the acceleration model, solve the event condition,",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 781.6439957275588,
      "end": 782.5839981689651,
      "text": "and then check the graph.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 783.3240036621291,
      "end": 786.3119978637916,
      "text": "That routine is far more dependable than hunting for a formula that merely",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 786.3119978637916,
      "end": 786.4800000000243,
      "text": "looks familiar.",
      "chapter": 5
    }
  ]
}
